  "frozenPublicHeadObligations": [
    {
      "id": "B01",
      "line": 19,
      "reason": "Exact transparent old natural ceiling height plus1/2; no integer strict wall is substituted."
    },
    {
      "id": "B02",
      "line": 23,
      "reason": "Halfheight divided by sqrt(n), with real total division at0; only positive-time tails are used for cancellation."
    },
    {
      "id": "B03",
      "line": 27,
      "reason": "Exact exp(pi^2/(8*c^3))-1; positivity proved under c>0."
    },
    {
      "id": "B04",
      "line": 30,
      "reason": "Constructs actual Rademacher coordinate IdentDistrib from qualified canonical law facts; exact Nat.ceil(m+1/2)=m+1 proves strict delta1/2. Bounded rounding error, cube/sixth-root identities and explicit positive tails derive height->infinity, n/height^2->infinity, n/height^3->1/c^3, point->0 and point*n^(1/6)->c. Qualified actual original strict S4 yields a positive-tail actual quotient divided by exp(correction)->1; correction->pi^2/(8*c^3), hence actual quotient and absolute error have the frozen limits. No zero denominator cancellation occurs."
    },
    {
      "id": "B05",
      "line": 283,
      "reason": "For arbitrary real endpoint a(n)<1 and n>0, strict event is subset of actual weak event. Finite real-measure monotonicity and nonnegative Brownian F give0<=strict ratio<=weak ratio even if F=0. The strict error is at most the qualified proper weak supremum plus1. Midpoint nonemptiness and this finite bound precede isLUB_csSup; result gives nonnegativity and pointwise domination without requiring a(n)>0."
    },
    {
      "id": "B06",
      "line": 370,
      "reason": "Qualified weak obstruction contributes only c>0, StrictMono subsequence and old critical-point open-window membership. The new halfpoint exceeds old point at n>0, and B04 makes it tend0, so it stays in the same original window eventually. B04 supplies a new strict positive gap; B05 gives eventual strict supremum>=gap/2. Old weak ratio/gap limits are discarded."
    },
    {
      "id": "B07",
      "line": 418,
      "reason": "Contraposition: B06 gap/2 lower bound contradicts convergence0 along its strictly increasing subsequence. Statement allows arbitrary real a and asserts necessity for the one fixed canonical Rademacher law, not every fixed law."
    },
    {
      "id": "B08",
      "line": 436,
      "reason": "At each prescribed sample universe, instantiate universal premise by the qualified ULift infinite-product Rademacher family. Its mean0/third moment/second integral1/iid/AE facts are actual qualified types. Convert literal maximum to prefix event only eventually n>=1 and use B07. Reverse implication uses exact qualified A sufficiency for every fixed family; law is outside n limit, no sup over laws or extra moment/regularity premise."
    }
  ],
